.TH MD2HTML-UC 1 "August 6, 2026" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
md2html-uiuc \- Convert Markdown to HTML with University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign theme
.SH SYNOPSIS
md2html-uiuc INPUT_FILE
.SH DESCRIPTION
md2html-uiuc is an easy-to-use wrapper script that converts a Markdown file to HTML using the UIUC-themed converter. It applies the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign branding (navy #13294B, orange #E84A27), enables wiki-link resolution from your wiki directory, and generates a hamburger navigation menu built from your wiki index.md.

This is a simplified interface to the underlying md2html.py script with commonly used options pre-configured for UIUC documentation workflows.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fBINPUT_FILE\fP
Path to the Markdown file to convert. Must have .md extension.
.SH BEHAVIOR
The script converts INPUT_FILE to an HTML file with the same basename in the same directory (e.g., notes.md → notes.html). It uses the following md2html.py options:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\fB--standalone\fP: Generate a full HTML document with header
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-s\fP: Enable wiki-link resolution
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-d ~/wiki\fP: Specify wiki directory for link resolution
.IP \(bu 2
\fB-n\fP: Generate navigation bar from wiki index.md
.RE
If an output file already exists, it will be overwritten without warning.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Convert a single Markdown file:
    md2html-uiuc meeting_notes.md
    # Creates meeting_notes.html in the same directory
.PP
Convert a file in a subdirectory:
    md2html-uiuc docs/project_overview.md
    # Creates docs/project_overview.html
.SH ENVIRONMENT
No specific environment variables are required. The script assumes:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Python 3 is available in PATH
.IP \(bu 2
Your wiki is located at ~/wiki (for wiki-link resolution and nav bar)
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/md2html.py\fP
The underlying Markdown to HTML converter (pure Python, stdlib only).
.TP
\fI~/md2html-uiuc\fP
This wrapper script.
.TP
\fI~/wiki/\fP
Your wiki directory (used for wiki-link resolution and navigation bar).
.TP
\fIINPUT_FILE.html\fP
The generated HTML output file (same directory as input).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0   Success.
1   Error (e.g., missing input file, missing md2html.py, or conversion failure).
